# Contributing to PROJECT_NAME

Thank you for helping. This page lists what a change needs before review.

## Set up

1. Install PREREQUISITES (exact versions are in the lockfile and dev container).
2. Run `BOOTSTRAP_COMMAND`; it installs from the lockfile and the Git hooks.
3. Run `GATE_COMMAND` once to confirm a clean baseline.

Opening the repository in the dev container gives the same toolchain as CI.

## Propose a change

- For a bug, open an issue with the bug form, or send a pull request with a
  failing test.
- For a new feature, a breaking change or a new dependency, open an issue to
  agree on the approach before writing much code.
- Security problems are never reported in public; see [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md).

## Make the change

- Keep each pull request to one purpose; include tests and documentation for
  changed behavior in the same pull request.
- Add a regression test that fails without the fix.
- Change dependencies only through the manifest and lockfile.
- Follow the existing style; the formatter and linter are authoritative.
- Write commit messages as [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/).

## Before requesting review

- `GATE_COMMAND` passes locally after your last edit.
- The pull request description lists the commands you ran and their results,
  and anything you could not verify.
- User-visible changes have a changelog entry.

## Review

Maintainers aim to respond within RESPONSE_TARGET. Code owners review changes
to the paths they own. A maintainer merges after required checks pass.

